.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt OI-APPLE-UPDATE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm oi-apple-update
.Nd install the OI-Apple packages an Intel Mac needs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n1
.Op Fl R Ar root
.Op Fl g Ar origin
.Op Fl m Ar model
.Op Ar group ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the Mac's model from
.Xr smbios 8
and its graphics devices from
.Xr prtconf 8 ,
chooses the group packages
.Pq Sy group/apple/ Ns Ar group
for it from
.Pa /usr/share/oi-apple/models.conf ,
and installs them with
.Sy metapackages/oi-apple
from the publisher
.Sy oi-local
into a new boot environment.
It stops when the running OS build is not the one oi-local's kernel
packages were built for.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl n
Show the plan and what
.Xr pkg 1
would do; change nothing.
.It Fl 1
Activate the new boot environment for the next boot only
.Pq Sy beadm activate -t .
.It Fl R Ar root
Install into the image at
.Ar root
instead of a new boot environment.
.It Fl g Ar origin
Add an origin to oi-local: a
.Pa .p5p
archive, a repository directory or an http(s) URL.
Default: the OI-Apple archive on mounted media
.Pq Pa /.cdrom/oi-apple/*.p5p .
.It Fl m Ar model
Use this model instead of the one
.Xr smbios 8
reports.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /usr/share/oi-apple/models.conf
models, PCI devices and groups; the osnet build
.It Pa /usr/share/oi-apple/unlock.list
packages whose version-lock facet is turned off
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success or when there is nothing to do, 1 on errors, 2 on usage errors.
